.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH view-key 1  "view-key " 
.SH NAME
view\-key \- Display information about a key file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBview\-key\fR [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlock a key file (default ~/.local/share/hs/keys/default.hskey, override
with \-k) and print its algorithm variants, fingerprint, and path, followed
by the armored public key. The passphrase is prompted unless
\-\-no\-passphrase or \-\-passphrase\-file is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Path to the secret key file (.hskey)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR
Use an empty passphrase (no prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fI<PASSPHRASE_FILE>\fR
Read the passphrase from a file (first line)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
